<v Alex Blumberg>It turns out there are a lot of Susan Jordans who don't remember me. A lot. One guy even called his ex-wife, a former Susan Jordan, and then called me back to tell me she'd never heard of me. I was getting nowhere by myself.
<v Alex Blumberg>事实证明有很多叫苏珊·乔丹的人都不记得我。很多。甚至有一个人打电话问了他前妻——一个叫苏珊·乔丹的人，然后回电告诉我她从来没听说过我。我一个人什么进展都没有。

00:39:57.980 --> 00:40:09.330
<v Alex Blumberg>So I contacted a professional. One Irving Botwinick, a certified New York City private investigator. Three days after putting him on the case, I got a message saying he'd found her. I called him back.
<v Alex Blumberg>所以我联系了一位专业人士。欧文·波特威尼克，一位持有执照的纽约私人侦探。在他接手案件三天后，我收到消息说他找到她了。我给他打了回去。

00:40:09.330 --> 00:40:54.040
<v Irving Botwinick>I called her this morning early. Roughly around 7:30. I said, good morning. I'd like to introduce myself. I said my name is so-and-so, and I'm a licensed private investigator in New York, and I'm looking for someone that used to live in Cincinnati, and went to a particular school there, and her name at the time was Susan Jordan. And she said, that's me. And I said, OK. And I said, do you know anybody named Alex Blumberg. And right away she, yeah. I babysat for him. And the interesting part about the whole thing is she definitely likes you, remembers you, and she's going to call you.
<v Irving Botwinick>我今天一早给她打了电话。大约在7:30左右。我说，早上好。我想自我介绍一下。我说我叫某某，我是纽约的一名持照私人侦探，我正在寻找一个过去住在辛辛那提，当时上过某所学校，名字叫苏珊·乔丹的人。她说，那是我。我说，OK。我说，你认识一个叫亚历克斯·布卢姆伯格的人吗。她立刻就说，嗯，我给他当过保姆。整个事情最有趣的部分是，她真的很喜欢你，记得你，而且她会给你打电话。

00:40:54.040 --> 00:40:57.790
<v Alex Blumberg>Hello, is this Susan?
<v Alex Blumberg>你好，是苏珊吗？

00:40:57.790 --> 00:41:00.590
<v Susan  Jordan>Yeah.
<v Susan  Jordan>是的。

00:41:00.590 --> 00:41:02.460
<v Alex Blumberg>This is Alex Blumberg.
<v Alex Blumberg>我是亚历克斯·布卢姆伯格。

00:41:02.460 --> 00:41:04.050
<v Susan Jordan>Hi, Alex. How are you doing?
<v Susan Jordan>嗨，亚历克斯。你好吗？

00:41:04.050 --> 00:41:05.410
<v Alex Blumberg>I'm doing OK. How are you?
<v Alex Blumberg>我很好。你呢？

